![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

When loading parsed files (such as JSON), we should validate the parsed file shape, record malformed entry diagnostics, skip bad entries, and pass those diagnostics into the package validator to ensure it fails closed. Currently, `inputs.rightsOverlay` is loaded but its shape is never validated.

```javascript
  const inputs = options.inputs ?? loadInputs(root, paths, diagnostics);
  if (inputs.rightsOverlay !== null && inputs.rightsOverlay !== undefined) {
    if (typeof inputs.rightsOverlay !== 'object' || Array.isArray(inputs.rightsOverlay)) {
      diagnostics.push({
        code: 'malformed_input_file',
        role: 'source_figure_asset_rights_display_policy',
        path: paths.rightsOverlayIn,
        reason: 'rights_overlay_is_not_an_object',
        severity: 'critical',
      });
    }
  }
  const rawRows = visualInventoryRows(inputs.visualInventory, paths, diagnostics);
  const rows = validVisualRows(rawRows, diagnostics);
```

